  "connectGuideTitle": "How to connect",
  "@connectGuideTitle": {"description": "Link under the gateway URL in Settings, and the title of the setup guide it opens."},
  "connectGuideBody": "Pomelu connects to Hermes Agent on your own computer. Do these steps one time.\n\n### 1. Install Hermes Agent\nInstall [Hermes Agent](https://hermes-agent.nousresearch.com/docs/getting-started/installation) 0.21.5 or newer on your computer. To update it:\n\n```\nhermes update\n```\n\n### 2. Set a username and password\nAdd these lines to `~/.hermes/.env` on the computer. Use your own username and a strong password:\n\n```\nHERMES_DASHBOARD_BASIC_AUTH_USERNAME=me\nHERMES_DASHBOARD_BASIC_AUTH_PASSWORD=a-strong-password\nHERMES_DASHBOARD_BASIC_AUTH_SECRET=paste-the-secret-here\n```\n\nTo make the secret, run:\n\n```\nopenssl rand -base64 32\n```\n\n### 3. Start the gateway\nRun this on the computer and keep it running:\n\n```\nhermes dashboard --host 0.0.0.0 --no-open\n```\n\n### 4. Find the address\n- **Same Wi-Fi:** `http://` + the computer's IP address + `:9119`, for example `http://192.168.1.20:9119`.\n- **Away from home:** use a private network such as [Tailscale](https://tailscale.com), or put the gateway behind `https://`.\n\n### 5. Connect the app\nIn Settings, type the address in **Gateway URL**. Sign in with the username and password. Tap **Test connection**, then **Save and connect**.\n\n### If it does not connect\n- **HTTP failed:** check the address. Make sure the computer is on and its firewall allows port 9119.\n- **WebSocket failed:** a proxy or tunnel in front of the gateway must allow WebSockets.\n- **Gateway too old:** run `hermes update` on the computer.",
  "@connectGuideBody": {"description": "Setup guide in Markdown: how to run a Hermes gateway the app can reach. Keep the code blocks, commands, file paths and variable names as they are."},
